    </resources>
    <!-- The sound driver runs on the 68000 (as in sonic1.xml): the vertical-blank interrupt calls two routines once a frame (0x6C0AA for the
         FM channels, 0x6CC16 for the PSG) and the driver writes the YM2612 and the PSG itself. The Z80 only plays sampled sounds, with a
         small program that the game copies into the Z80 RAM when it starts (0x61E4). The game starts a song (0x6C064), an effect (0x6C08E)
         or a sequence of the PSG (0x6CBDA) by calling a subroutine with the number in D0 (D1 for the PSG): <driver requests> lists them, a
         track says which one takes its number with request="...". The header of the game says Japan. -->
    <driver m68k_init="0x61E4 0x6C000 0x6CBC2" m68k_frame="0x6C0AA 0x6CC16" requests="0x6C064 0x6C08E 0x6CBDA" warmup_frames="4" region="japan" cart_crc32="1ab9a5de"/>
